(867, 1, '2024-08-29 07:34:58', '2024-08-29 06:34:58', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Norsworthy Farms and Agro Allied Industries Limited has inaugurated a 10-metric-tonne per hour palm oil mill in Akwukwu, Igbo, Delta State.</p>\n<p>The event was attended state governor, Sherriff Oborevwori, former Delta State Governor,  Dr. Ifeanyi Okowa, among other dignitaries.</p>\n<p>The Chairman of Norsworthy Farms and Agro Allied Industries Limited, Dr. Gabriel Ogbechie, lamented Nigeria’s reduced prominence in palm oil production, highlighting its transition from a net exporter to a net importer.</p>\n<p>He said, “With an annual consumption of approximately N2.5m metric tonnes and an import expenditure of $500m per annum, the country faces a significant deficit. He noted that despite vast suitable plantation land, only a fraction is utilised, primarily through manual processing techniques by small-scale farmers.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Norsworthy Farms unveils palm oil mill', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'norsworthy-farms-unveils-palm-oil-mill', '', '', '2024-08-31 00:00:10', '2024-08-30 23:00:10', '', 0, 'http://tplabs.co/agrios/?p=867', 0, 'post', '', 0),
